
===== Column Segment Router

Some deployments use compound identifiers that combine two parts with a delimiter, such as a location code made up of a region code
and a sequence number (e.g. `100-001`). The Column Segment router splits such a compound value on a delimiter and compares a single
segment of it to a value on the other side, without needing a custom BSH or Java router.

.The following configuration parameters are supported.
[IMPORTANT]
====

sourceColumn:: The name of the captured row column to read, or the literal token `:EXTERNAL_DATA` to read the row's external data instead.
Required.
nodeProperty:: The node property to compare against: `externalId`, `nodeId`, or `nodeGroupId`. Optional, defaults to `externalId`.
matchMode:: Which side gets split: `COLUMN` (split the source), `NODE_PROPERTY` (split the node property), or `BOTH` (split both,
using separate delimiters). Required.
delimiter:: The delimiter used to split the source in `COLUMN`/`BOTH` mode, or the node property in `NODE_PROPERTY` mode. Required.
nodePropertyDelimiter:: The delimiter used to split the node property in `BOTH` mode. Required only when `matchMode=BOTH`.
segmentIndex:: The zero-based segment index to compare after splitting. Optional, defaults to `0`.
wildcard:: An optional value that, when it equals the full, unsplit source value, means "send to all nodes". Defaults to `*`.
====

NOTE: The set of candidate nodes is split and indexed once per routing pass and cached for its duration, so only the row's source
value needs to be split on each row.

Consider an `ITEM_ID` column holding a compound value of the form `<regionCode>-<sequence>` (e.g. `100-001`) that needs to be routed to
a region node whose external ID holds only the unsplit region code (e.g. `100`):

.Router Expression

----
sourceColumn=ITEM_ID nodeProperty=externalId matchMode=COLUMN delimiter=-
----

Consider the opposite case: a `REGION_CODE` column holding the unsplit region code (e.g. `100`) that needs to be routed to a node whose
external ID is the compound value (e.g. `100-001`):

.Router Expression

----
sourceColumn=REGION_CODE nodeProperty=externalId matchMode=NODE_PROPERTY delimiter=-
----

====== Migrating from a Custom BSH or Java Router

Custom BSH or Java routers that split a compound identifier and compare a segment of it to a node property or column can typically be
replaced by a single Column Segment router. For example, a BSH router that splits a column's value on `-` and compares the first segment
to the node's external ID might look like:

.Example BSH Router (before)
----
String[] parts = DATA.get("ITEM_ID").split("-");
targetNode = parts[0].equals(EXTERNAL_ID);
----

This can be replaced with a Column Segment router expression, removing the need for a BSH interpreter on every row and allowing the
candidate node set to be indexed once per routing pass instead of split on every row:

.Equivalent Column Segment Router Expression (after)
----
sourceColumn=ITEM_ID nodeProperty=externalId matchMode=COLUMN delimiter=-
----
